; MX1 the effective address's heads (docs/v35s-mechanisms.md section 3.5: the ROM has no EA
; routine; the EA's clocks are the displacement bytes' pops and one add). A memory routine's
; first word is the add (ea=BI: the ModR/M mode's base on port A + its index on port B + the
; popped displacement into the address register, the default segment SS for a BP mode); the
; pops come before it, in the heads below. The word after E of a ModR/M memory cell dispatches
; to the head of the registered ModR/M byte's mode with the routine's entry in the return
; register (the dispatch's call: the V20 loader's mode branch, S_D8 / S_D16, before the
; routine's first row, v30-structure.md section 6); the head pops and returns. No head reads a
; register or posts: the pops alone, and the book's EA clock where they leave one.
;
; Two sets, by the routine's header (the decode table's eab bit for its cells):
;   ea=book  the book's EA: 3 clocks at mod 00 and 01 and for the direct address, 4 at mod 10
;            (v35_book_clocks.json EA_values). Each mode's pops and the add, and the book clock
;            they do not fill as an OPEN word; at mod 00 (the add alone against the book's 3)
;            one OPEN word, the second clock a book error: silicon's EA table puts [reg] and
;            [base+index] one clock under every d8 form, where the book charges EA 3 for both
;            (docs/v35s-eu-timing.md M4: +0 / +1 / +2).
;   ea=bare  the pops alone (mod 00 enters the routine's add directly): for the routines whose
;            own acts already exceed the book's clocks after the EA (the store's datum read
;            behind the add's two ports, the RMW's write post), so that no path carries an OPEN
;            word beyond the book.

routine eab0 diff=m00:-1 why="book error of one at mod 00 (the add one clock, the book's EA 3): docs/v35s-eu-timing.md M4, [reg] and [base+index] +0 against any + d8 +1 where the book charges EA 3 for both; one book clock stays (OPEN)"
    open ret                                ; OPEN: the book's EA clock at mod 00 the add does not fill; return to the routine's add

routine eab8
    pop=dl                                  ; pop the displacement byte (d8)
    open ret                                ; OPEN: the book's EA clock at mod 01 the pop and the add do not fill (EA 3); return to the add

routine eab16
    pop=dl                                  ; pop the displacement's low byte (d16)
    pop=dh                                  ; pop its high byte
    open ret                                ; OPEN: the book's EA clock at mod 10 the pops and the add do not fill (EA 4); return to the add

routine ea8
    pop=dl ret                              ; pop the displacement byte (d8); return to the routine's add

; the direct address (mod 00 rm 110) in both sets (its two pops and the add are the book's EA 3),
; and mod 10 in the bare set
routine ead
    pop=dl                                  ; pop the displacement's (the direct address's) low byte
    pop=dh ret                              ; pop its high byte; return to the routine's add
